; Journal for test/regress/balance-assignment-lot-amount.test.  It cannot be
; that file's inline journal: the Lean oracle that test/semantic/check_all.py
; runs reads an annotated target such as "= 12 AAPL {$100.00}" as a target
; for the whole AAPL holding, where ledger assigns only the {$100.00} lot,
; and check_all.py fails on any inline positive journal the oracle
; disagrees with.

2024/01/01 Opening
    Assets:Broker              3 AAPL
    Assets:Broker              2 AAPL {$90.00}
    Assets:Cash

2024/01/02 Single lot left over
    Assets:Broker              = 3 AAPL
    Equity:Adjustments

2024/01/03 Two lots
    Assets:Stocks              10 AAPL {$100.00}
    Assets:Stocks              5 AAPL {$110.00}
    Assets:Cash

2024/01/04 Several lots
    Assets:Stocks              = 20 AAPL
    Equity:Adjustments

2024/01/05 Annotated target
    Assets:Stocks              = 12 AAPL {$100.00}
    Equity:Adjustments

2024/01/06 Other commodity
    Assets:Broker              = 5 EUR
    Equity:Adjustments

2024/01/07 Annotated other lot
    Assets:Stocks              = 3 AAPL {$120.00}
    Equity:Adjustments

2024/01/08 Annotated zero
    Assets:Stocks              = 0 AAPL {$100.00}
    Equity:Adjustments
